From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 20:17:21 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] signal: skip the write-strip region query on a read SIGBUS

bus_handler asks for the faulting page's host protection (a
mach_vm_region call) on every SIGBUS whose target is readable, to see
whether the host stripped a write wine wants. Only a write can find
that, and the answer was used only by a write; a read paid the Mach
call for a sampled log line.

Every guest split lock (an x86 lock xadd or xchg across a 16-byte
boundary, which FEX completes) is such a read: an alignment fault
reports WnR=0 (esr 0x92000021). Jurassic World Evolution's protected
code runs about 14,000 a second, and the split-lock probe measures 61
to 75 us an operation. A read now skips the query; its sampled
[wr-strip] line shows host_prot=-1. What the handler does is unchanged.

Class: diagnostics
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-12-guest-split-locks.md
Offered-upstream: no; the SIGBUS handler is the iOS port's
---
 build/ntdll-unix/signal_arm64_ios.c | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/build/ntdll-unix/signal_arm64_ios.c b/build/ntdll-unix/signal_arm64_ios.c
index fdcabe6..4fe6d61 100644
--- a/build/ntdll-unix/signal_arm64_ios.c
+++ b/build/ntdll-unix/signal_arm64_ios.c
@@ -12656,7 +12656,12 @@ static void bus_handler( int signal, siginfo_t *siginfo, void *sigcontext )
                 mach_port_t ro = MACH_PORT_NULL;
                 int host_prot = -1;
 
-                if (mach_vm_region( mach_task_self(), &ra, &rs, VM_REGION_BASIC_INFO_64,
+                /* PLA-242: only a write can find its write stripped, so a read
+                 * (every guest split lock: an alignment fault reports WnR=0) skips
+                 * the region query, a Mach call on each of them; its sampled
+                 * [wr-strip] line shows host_prot=-1. */
+                if (is_write &&
+                    mach_vm_region( mach_task_self(), &ra, &rs, VM_REGION_BASIC_INFO_64,
                                     (vm_region_info_t)&rbi, &rc, &ro ) == KERN_SUCCESS)
                     host_prot = rbi.protection;
 
